                    leading_pulse:          `Engagement pulse, volunteering participation and manager-behaviour ratings — they move before the business outcomes`,
                    leading_hours:          `Training hours delivered and volunteering days run — easy to count and looks busy`,
                    leading_csatnow:        `Just watch CSAT and attrition directly — wait for the lagging numbers to move`,
                    control_phased:         `Phased rollout — treat the at-risk sites first, untreated sites act as a comparison group against a baseline`,
                    control_baseline:       `Set a baseline and re-measure later — assume any improvement is ours, no comparison group`,
                    control_none:           `No baseline or control — roll out everywhere at once and claim the headline improvement`,
                    roi_avoided:            `If attrition falls X points we avoid EUR Y in replacement cost (€9,500/leaver) AND protect EUR 32M of contract revenue`,
                    roi_engagement:         `Engagement rose, so the programme worked — engagement is the return in itself`,
